WEBVTT

00:04.180 --> 00:05.360
Those are...

00:05.850 --> 00:08.720
Magic circles for gates
like we saw on floor 11?

00:09.030 --> 00:10.160
It can't be!

00:12.870 --> 00:14.160
Help!

00:15.540 --> 00:17.540
Go this way! That way's dangerous!

00:15.540 --> 00:17.540
Th-Those are Dinoboroses!

00:17.540 --> 00:20.790
Why are monsters from deep in
the dungeon up here on the surface?!

00:22.790 --> 00:25.460
Clairie Serah

00:23.020 --> 00:25.460
Rodge! I'll cast some barriers!
Incant on the double!

00:25.460 --> 00:27.300
Fire Faction
Rodge Holland

00:25.900 --> 00:26.890
We're counting on you!

00:26.890 --> 00:28.220
Prepare to counterattack!

00:37.930 --> 00:40.110
Keridos Gardinas!

00:47.530 --> 00:49.060
Begin incantations!

00:49.060 --> 00:52.100
Leave the front line
to Clairie's guardians!

00:53.160 --> 00:54.710
Let's take these out in one swoop!

00:55.660 --> 00:57.340
Freyd Raechel!

01:01.860 --> 01:04.710
How in the world
are there so many guardians?

01:05.670 --> 01:08.050
They've crushed this surprise
attack in an instant!

01:08.330 --> 01:09.330
Behold...

01:10.480 --> 01:12.800
high mages of the tower.

01:13.950 --> 01:17.740
The capital is under the protection of the
Magia Vander. To think you'd sully it...

01:17.740 --> 01:19.350
What fools.

01:19.780 --> 01:22.340
Investigate the origin
of those magic circles!

01:22.340 --> 01:24.610
Someone was behind
setting these monsters loose!

01:24.610 --> 01:25.990
Capture them without fail!

01:29.500 --> 01:32.070
It survived that simultaneous attack?

01:32.070 --> 01:34.740
How infuriating. Stop causing trouble!

01:44.250 --> 01:47.640
Burn to ash! Eltorias Gardelshing!

01:49.550 --> 01:51.110
Rodge, run!

02:05.610 --> 02:09.980
Magic doesn't work on this thing?
No... It's nullifying it?!

02:09.980 --> 02:11.360
What about my guardians?

02:18.700 --> 02:21.410
That sword... No way!

02:21.410 --> 02:22.720
A mage slayer?!

02:23.290 --> 02:25.960
Rigarden Magical Academy

02:23.870 --> 02:25.960
We cannot stop the monster invasion!

02:26.280 --> 02:28.280
Tower guards are headed into the city,

02:28.280 --> 02:29.960
but they're already half wiped out!

02:29.960 --> 02:31.710
There are also civilian casualties!

02:31.710 --> 02:34.100
What <i>are</i> those things?

02:31.760 --> 02:37.180
Rigarden Magical Academy Headmistress
Caldron Anouve

02:34.100 --> 02:37.290
That mage slayer Finn
and the others brought back...

02:37.720 --> 02:41.740
Have they been mass-produced
and deployed directly into battle?

02:41.740 --> 02:43.500
Given our foe is using gates,

02:43.500 --> 02:48.060
could this be the same culprit who
appeared during the all-student praxis?

02:48.400 --> 02:51.220
Still, this could not have been
carried out by a lone perpetrator.

02:51.220 --> 02:53.720
It's far too systematic.

02:53.720 --> 02:57.750
To time the attack right
at the conclusion of Terminalia...

02:57.750 --> 02:59.340
What is the enemy after?

02:59.340 --> 03:00.640
Headmistress Caldron!

03:00.640 --> 03:02.450
The academy should send forces into town!

03:02.450 --> 03:03.250
We will not!

03:08.580 --> 03:11.750
As I thought, the horde
in the capital is a diversion.

03:11.750 --> 03:13.760
Defend the tower!

03:14.910 --> 03:18.260
So we are the enemy's
true objective, are we?

03:19.230 --> 03:21.330
After casting the Great Barrier,

03:21.330 --> 03:24.770
Lady Elfaria's magic is largely depleted,
the same as the rest of you.

03:24.930 --> 03:28.480
Ellenor Ljos Alf

03:25.310 --> 03:32.230
Terminalia is the only day of the year
when all of the Magia Vander are weakened.

03:28.520 --> 03:32.230
Zeo Thorzeus Reinbolt

03:32.320 --> 03:34.990
Cariot Incindia Wiseman

03:32.690 --> 03:34.990
I don't know where these
idiots have come from,

03:34.990 --> 03:36.920
but that must be why they're here.

03:35.030 --> 03:37.490
Elfaria Albis Serfort

03:37.490 --> 03:40.990
Lord Cariot, it would be prudent
to serve as reinforcements.

03:38.740 --> 03:43.660
Fire Faction Aide-de-Camp
Logwell

03:40.990 --> 03:43.740
As things stand,
innocent civilians will be sacrificed.

03:44.170 --> 03:46.550
The power of the Magia Vander
should immediately be—

03:46.550 --> 03:48.620
Silence, Logwell.

03:49.880 --> 03:55.440
Or do you want your windpipe gouged out
like your eyes were? You fool.

03:50.460 --> 03:55.710
Aaron Masterias Oldking

03:55.440 --> 03:59.240
Do nothing you are not asked to do.
You are a disgrace to us.

03:59.890 --> 04:02.790
Then what <i>are</i> we supposed to do, old man?

04:02.790 --> 04:04.890
Watch from afar and pass judgment?

04:04.890 --> 04:06.770
Just so.

04:07.350 --> 04:10.770
I forbid the Magia Vander
from leaving this place.

04:11.240 --> 04:17.400
If a wand falls, and the Great Barrier
is lost, the Celestial Host will invade.

04:18.180 --> 04:23.400
Then it won't just be Rigarden,
but all the world rendered ash and dust.

04:24.160 --> 04:27.910
That is the one thing that
must not come to pass.

04:28.980 --> 04:32.670
Those blasted Magia Vander
aren't coming out.

04:33.000 --> 04:35.800
And after all the bait
we set out for them, too!

04:35.800 --> 04:39.500
If they'd just saunter on out here,
we could take them down.

04:39.500 --> 04:42.050
In that case, let's enjoy what we have...

04:42.050 --> 04:44.390
This magnificent spectacle!

04:45.550 --> 04:46.560
Say it isn't so!

04:47.170 --> 04:50.060
The people...
The treasures of the capital!

04:50.060 --> 04:52.450
The talent capable of confronting the sky!

04:53.060 --> 04:56.530
We can't... let this happen.

04:56.530 --> 04:58.690
Mama!

05:03.450 --> 05:04.950
Allume Yris!

05:08.580 --> 05:09.830
Wait!

05:19.980 --> 05:21.400
Will!

05:39.990 --> 05:44.700
Episode 14
The Party from Hell Begins

06:55.820 --> 06:59.610
Why is this world so unkind?

07:00.260 --> 07:02.670
Why is it so cruel to swords?

07:03.260 --> 07:05.260
I've had those thoughts before.

07:05.900 --> 07:08.560
I'd be lying if I said I didn't resent it.

07:09.260 --> 07:10.160
And yet...

07:13.870 --> 07:16.870
I've never wished for anything like this!

07:27.140 --> 07:28.390
Stop shaking!

07:28.800 --> 07:31.890
The more scared you are,
the more people die!

07:40.400 --> 07:41.450
Will!

07:42.110 --> 07:44.190
Go for the ones with weapons!

07:46.120 --> 07:47.780
Crysto Wreath!

07:49.600 --> 07:53.160
We mages can handle the ones
that aren't carrying swords!

07:54.040 --> 07:54.790
Understood!

08:06.870 --> 08:08.330
If Will's here...

08:09.250 --> 08:12.380
If he's here,
he can defeat the mage slayers!

08:13.000 --> 08:15.960
But he can't take them all by himself.

08:15.960 --> 08:17.480
There are simply too many!

08:20.190 --> 08:23.900
Iris, I hereby grant you my authority.

08:23.900 --> 08:28.150
Call the dwarves to action.
Put a stop to this savagery.

08:29.210 --> 08:31.480
Thank you, Lord Aaron.

08:33.160 --> 08:37.040
On behalf of the great Masterias Noah,
I, a watcher, command you!

08:37.040 --> 08:39.290
Gordvere! Gordvere!

08:39.290 --> 08:42.210
The ban on combat by dwarves
is hereby lifted!

08:42.210 --> 08:46.080
Mages, coordinate with the dwarves
and eliminate all monsters!

08:46.730 --> 08:48.020
I repeat!

08:48.020 --> 08:50.220
Order: Gordvere!

08:51.110 --> 08:52.360
Everyone!

08:53.390 --> 08:55.350
I beg you! Please lend us your strength!

08:57.810 --> 09:02.260
Putting us to work like this right at the
start of the new year? Blasted mages.

09:02.260 --> 09:04.260
Quit your bellyaching and let's go!

09:04.260 --> 09:07.360
Everyone, we're going
to save Will and the others!

09:07.360 --> 09:09.610
Yeah!

09:09.610 --> 09:11.240
Dax Darbicans!

09:13.990 --> 09:16.860
Leave the armed monsters to the dwarves!

09:16.860 --> 09:19.500
Mages, target all other attackers!

09:19.500 --> 09:22.460
Students, we are putting you to work, too.

09:22.460 --> 09:25.880
We're shorthanded, so I don't care
if you're a burden to the rest of us.

09:25.880 --> 09:28.380
Become a wand that protects the people!

09:29.030 --> 09:30.780
He's asking for our help, but...

09:30.780 --> 09:34.010
Those things can take down high mages.
What are we supposed to do?

09:34.320 --> 09:37.230
Owen Sique: Lisolde Dua!

09:38.520 --> 09:40.520
I-Incredible!

09:43.540 --> 09:46.990
Even using enchantments,
I couldn't take it down in one blow!

09:46.990 --> 09:48.980
So this is a monster from the deep.

09:49.320 --> 09:50.440
Moreover...

09:54.940 --> 09:58.620
any magic that comes within a certain
distance of that weapon gets dispelled.

09:59.550 --> 10:00.870
Is it nullifying the magic?

10:01.330 --> 10:03.480
Or is it absorbing the magical energy?

10:03.480 --> 10:06.410
Either way, it's lethal for mages.

10:06.910 --> 10:09.140
If there's a way to overcome it,
it'd have to be...

10:09.140 --> 10:09.880
Lihanna!

10:10.170 --> 10:11.540
Don't do anything crazy!

10:11.540 --> 10:14.550
Colette, can you do
what I'm about to tell you?

10:14.550 --> 10:15.680
Huh?

10:16.050 --> 10:17.860
What?!

10:18.600 --> 10:20.560
Alfs Ringhul!

10:22.430 --> 10:24.940
Even illusion magic gets negated?

10:24.940 --> 10:28.380
We can't hold out here
until the dwarves arrive!

10:28.380 --> 10:32.060
Once Lihanna and the rest of our vanguard
is exhausted, we're done for, too!

10:32.060 --> 10:33.900
Running is our only option!

10:33.900 --> 10:35.100
No.

10:35.100 --> 10:39.330
When the enemy disperses our magic,
it slows them down for just a moment.

10:39.900 --> 10:41.000
In which case...

10:41.620 --> 10:43.370
Fire off magic at random!

10:43.370 --> 10:46.120
It doesn't have to affect them!
We're just pinning them down!

10:46.120 --> 10:47.750
Verdes Lana!

10:46.120 --> 10:47.750
Glace Itier!

10:51.000 --> 10:53.260
More! We need more!

10:53.600 --> 10:55.260
Don't stop!

10:57.010 --> 10:59.430
That's right. This is enough.

10:59.830 --> 11:04.430
If we do this, then the other monsters
are forced to act as shields.

11:04.430 --> 11:05.690
And with that...

11:05.690 --> 11:07.940
Colette! Now!

11:11.050 --> 11:12.690
Saint Viola!

11:13.440 --> 11:16.450
I'm so sorry!

11:30.290 --> 11:34.070
Toppling the monument
of a former Magia Vander...

11:34.490 --> 11:36.550
That's sure to bring divine retribution.

11:36.550 --> 11:38.370
I see!

11:38.370 --> 11:41.810
They can't nullify physical objects
that carry no magic.

11:41.810 --> 11:46.180
Throw stones or anything else you can!
Earth mages, begin a barrage!

11:46.710 --> 11:49.190
Turn the unknown back
into the known, Rigarden!

11:50.530 --> 11:53.380
Those little academy
fledglings do good work.

11:53.380 --> 11:56.220
This year's tower hopefuls
are incredibly talented.

11:56.220 --> 11:57.820
I give you a full 100 points.

11:57.820 --> 12:00.450
Organize around the earth mages
and form a resistance!

12:00.450 --> 12:02.500
The dwarves will be here soon!

12:02.830 --> 12:06.300
It's galling that we have to rely
on the dwarves for help,

12:06.300 --> 12:07.830
but the end justifies the means.

12:09.720 --> 12:11.970
This place is under
the Magia Vanders' protection!

12:11.970 --> 12:13.840
We won't let it fall!

12:14.320 --> 12:17.330
That's Rigarden for you!
They're back on their feet.

12:17.330 --> 12:23.220
Their expedition running across the morons
working on the Sleime really hurt us.

12:23.760 --> 12:28.840
Masterias Noah and that one member of
the little people made off with a Sleime.

12:29.680 --> 12:32.150
What a thing to happen.

12:32.580 --> 12:37.150
Their dwarven support aside, one portion
of the mages adapted very quickly.

12:37.430 --> 12:40.240
Word of our secret weapon
must have gotten around.

12:40.660 --> 12:43.300
If the Upper Institute had
managed to analyze the Sleime

12:43.300 --> 12:46.410
and devise some countermeasure,
I couldn't bear to watch.

12:46.950 --> 12:52.740
We were forced to jump on the plan without
being able to produce them at scale.

12:52.740 --> 12:58.670
If they hadn't seen our hand,
it would've been the perfect surprise attack.

12:58.670 --> 13:03.080
Well, there do seem to be
a few other factors at play.

13:03.860 --> 13:07.140
Though I suppose we have no choice.
It's a little early...

13:08.740 --> 13:10.310
but here's our special treat.

13:17.710 --> 13:19.040
Is that...

13:19.040 --> 13:20.120
a gate?

13:20.780 --> 13:22.780
What is going on?!

14:08.150 --> 14:09.270
Now then...

14:09.860 --> 14:11.870
That's enough playing tag.

14:11.870 --> 14:15.460
You're the ones who made
that mage slayer, aren't you?

14:16.870 --> 14:19.530
You will cough up everything you know.

14:22.050 --> 14:23.690
It's already too late.

14:23.690 --> 14:28.270
Our role was to draw you
into the depths of the dungeon!

14:28.270 --> 14:30.610
By now, the surface is—

14:33.750 --> 14:34.910
That can't be.

14:36.190 --> 14:37.500
Mage Slayer Sword

14:37.690 --> 14:40.980
Mage Slayer Sword
"Indeed, this would kill all those self-important mages."
"Tower, delegate all investigation and analysis to me."
"Do not drag your heels in this. We haven't a moment to spare."
"Or perhaps you're hoping for a massive slaughter?"
-Director of the Upper Institute, Kreutz Harlon

14:42.690 --> 14:45.990
Gate
Teleportation magic devised by the Mage Queen. Constructing
an entrance allows anything to be transported to a preestablished exit.
Using one is extremely difficult. Anyone who can is either
a preternatural genius or an unnatural beast.

15:09.090 --> 15:12.390
How is it so strong? This is impossible!

15:14.170 --> 15:18.150
Don't tell me...
Is it even stronger than a Grand Duke?

15:18.650 --> 15:22.180
That thing is... a Devander?

15:22.180 --> 15:24.650
A notorious monster from floor 40.

15:25.010 --> 15:29.250
This creature has even killed previous
generations of Magia Vander!

15:29.660 --> 15:34.830
That beast killed fifty of our guys
just shoving it through a gate.

15:34.830 --> 15:37.670
It was quite a task
to take it alive, wasn't it?

15:37.670 --> 15:40.040
And now it's gonna go on a rampage for us!

15:43.630 --> 15:47.700
Even if I dodge a direct hit,
I get blown aside like a scrap of paper!

15:47.700 --> 15:50.260
This isn't an opponent
I can cross swords with head-on.

15:50.260 --> 15:51.880
Right now, all I can do is run!

16:03.260 --> 16:04.900
D-Don't...

16:08.810 --> 16:11.280
Th-The laggard? You...

16:11.610 --> 16:13.030
Run!

16:15.410 --> 16:18.020
Get out of here!

16:35.560 --> 16:36.980
Will!

16:38.980 --> 16:40.720
Are you all right, Will?

16:41.540 --> 16:43.230
Mister Donnan?

16:43.510 --> 16:45.360
You just sit tight.

16:45.360 --> 16:49.360
We're gonna crush that monster!

16:49.360 --> 16:53.230
Focus all fighting power in the south part
of the city around the book-learner!

16:53.230 --> 16:55.330
Defeating the Devander
is our top priority!

16:55.330 --> 16:59.690
Once the dwarves destroy its mage slayer,
launch a combined attack!

17:00.250 --> 17:01.670
Come on! Let's go!

17:01.670 --> 17:02.540
Right.

17:06.080 --> 17:08.900
Looks like they're swarming it.

17:08.900 --> 17:11.010
Indeed, it does seem that way.

17:11.010 --> 17:12.780
All according to plan.

17:14.820 --> 17:17.610
Now, eat your fill!

17:19.270 --> 17:21.520
Wh-What is this?

17:23.850 --> 17:26.020
It's pushing out its core?

17:30.140 --> 17:32.280
A trap? And we've been caught in it!

17:32.280 --> 17:33.980
Collect the traces from the monsters!

17:33.980 --> 17:36.090
Too late!

17:47.000 --> 17:52.180
The Devander has an unusual ability.
It can collect traces from other monsters.

17:52.450 --> 17:56.810
Basically, it consumes its own kin
to get crazy strong!

17:56.810 --> 17:58.810
Stop it from gathering any more!

17:58.810 --> 18:01.370
All hands, attack!

18:06.610 --> 18:08.320
Oh, no, you don't!

18:08.320 --> 18:11.860
You just sit there and watch
as this monster is born!

18:46.540 --> 18:48.370
It doesn't get any better than this!

18:48.370 --> 18:50.340
The mages' magic won't work on it!

18:50.340 --> 18:53.440
And the dwarves' ridiculous
strength doesn't do any good either!

18:54.110 --> 18:56.570
A whole horde of monsters
served as sacrifices for this.

18:56.860 --> 18:59.430
They used the attack on Rigarden...

18:59.430 --> 19:01.450
to strengthen their secret weapon?

19:02.910 --> 19:04.830
The party is a ceremony.

19:04.830 --> 19:06.710
The city is an altar.

19:07.150 --> 19:10.990
With the stage set, the killing
of the Magia Vander is at hand!

19:13.910 --> 19:15.680
It's too strong.

19:15.680 --> 19:19.100
The mages and dwarves
don't stand a chance!

19:19.450 --> 19:21.220
If I'm going to stop it...

19:21.570 --> 19:23.650
that power is the only way!

19:24.480 --> 19:26.100
Will! Your sword!

19:31.030 --> 19:32.230
Crysto Wreath!

19:51.960 --> 19:55.050
Rosty!

20:15.710 --> 20:19.300
Kiki, go to Miss Colette.

20:19.940 --> 20:23.310
I will protect your master.

20:24.160 --> 20:25.600
I promise you.

20:26.450 --> 20:28.430
So run along now.

20:36.570 --> 20:37.720
That's right.

20:38.270 --> 20:41.440
What I have to do is perfectly clear.

20:46.180 --> 20:48.550
No matter how angry I am, I can't best it.

20:49.200 --> 20:51.280
No matter how level-headed I am,

20:51.280 --> 20:53.440
no plan works against it!

20:54.040 --> 20:55.690
Not my wits or knowledge...

20:56.140 --> 20:58.130
Not the skills
I've drilled into my body...

20:58.130 --> 20:59.530
Not these pitiful feelings...

21:00.230 --> 21:04.780
In the face of this outrageous situation,
nothing I have is of any help at all.

21:10.010 --> 21:12.080
Which tells me I'm...

21:16.090 --> 21:18.460
I really am just...

21:27.560 --> 21:28.390
Huh?

21:29.780 --> 21:30.810
Will...

21:32.310 --> 21:34.060
I'll always be by your side.

23:28.090 --> 23:31.060
Wistoria: Wand and Sword

23:36.680 --> 23:39.700
Next time on <i>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</i>,

23:39.700 --> 23:42.850
episode 15, "One Single Magic Spell."

23:41.020 --> 23:46.030
Episode 15
One Single Magic Spell
